# =============================================================================
# Tarball exclusions.
#
# `files` in package.json whitelists whole directories (src/, scripts/), which is
# the right default — but a whitelisted DIRECTORY pulls in everything beneath it,
# including build detritus a local install or an agent dropped there. This file
# is the second gate.
#
# `yarn pack` and `npm pack` disagree about nested node_modules: yarn excludes it,
# npm does NOT when the parent directory is whitelisted in `files`. Publishing
# happens via `yarn npm publish`, so yarn's behaviour is what ships today — but
# relying on that is relying on an accident of tooling. The rules below make both
# commands produce the same tarball, and CI asserts it.
# =============================================================================

**/node_modules/

# wrangler local state, including the account identity file it writes on first
# login (account ID + the account's display name, usually an email address).
**/.wrangler/

# Agent tooling session state and local plans, wherever an agent's cwd dropped them.
**/.omc/
.omc/

# Local-only artifacts.
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
